# SS-04 - Seven causal rules and daily simulation engine
Workstream ID: SS-04
GitHub issue: https://github.com/Zanark/StonksSniper/issues/4
Status: DONE
Milestone: M1
Dependencies: SS-01

## Purpose
Provide explicit teaching rules and deterministic long/cash accounting over real observations.

## Tasks
- [x] Implement SMA, EMA, Wilder RSI, Donchian, Bollinger, MACD and body engulfing.
- [x] Execute previous-close targets only at next-session opens with fees/slippage.
- [x] Report marked equity, open units, drawdown, fill ledger and cost-matched benchmark.
- [x] Verify prefix invariance, warmup, final pending signals, edge inputs and costs.

## Acceptance criteria
- Future observations cannot alter earlier decisions/equity on a fixed input dataset.
- Every variant has exact rules, concept source and limits; no implied efficacy.

## Completion evidence
- src/stonks_sniper/patterns.py and engine.py implemented.
- Focused arithmetic/causality tests pass within the 37-test M1 suite.
- All seven variants ran over each of three real NSE/BSE datasets (21 simulations).
- Repeated identical-input runs agreed; fresh upstream requests are not immutable snapshots.
- Point-in-time source validity is a separate workstream. Human acceptance is not recorded.

## Completion log
- 2026-11-11: Implemented the bounded single-stock engine; no portfolio/short/leverage claim.
- 2026-11-11: Verified warmup, prefix invariance, next-session fills, final pending
  signals and accounting. Closed technical M1 scope, not research-quality qualification.
